Linux Basics I

Shared SSH lab with 42 stations under ~/challenges.

Login: user / user  (port 22)

How to play
  cd ~/challenges
  ls
  cat <station>/README

Practical stations
  Find a keyword in the lab, then run:
    ./checker '<keyword>'
  Wrong keyword prints an error. Correct keyword prints CN{...}.

Theory stations
  Run ./ask and answer each question. On success it prints the flag.

Safety (read this)
  You do NOT have sudo ALL. Do not expect passwordless root.
  checker and ask are execute-only binaries. You can run them; you cannot
  read or copy their contents (cat/strings/less should fail).
  Do not ship world-readable shell checkers that embed plaintext flags.
  Do not grant student accounts (ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL in any lab image.

Submit each CN{...} flag in the Hackploy UI for that challenge tile.
